To expand ({poly([2, 'x'], [3, ''])})({poly([1, 'x'], [-4, ''])}), multiply each term of the first bracket by each term of the second.
• {mono(2, 'x')} × x = {mono(2, 'x²')}
• {mono(2, 'x')} × {br(-4)} = {mono(-8, 'x')}
• {3} × x = {mono(3, 'x')}
• {3} × {br(-4)} = {-12}
Two terms times two terms always make four products. Then collect the like terms: {mono(-8, 'x')} + {mono(3, 'x')} = {mono(-5, 'x')}, so the answer is {quad(2, -5, -12)}.
